<title>USA: TWA cuts some airfares.</title>
<headline>TWA cuts some airfares.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trans World Airlines Inc said it cut fares on round trip domestic flights from 11 U.S. and Canadian cities and on flights to five international cities from New York.</p>
<p>The lowest domestic fares are available Tuesday, Wednesday and Saturday and the domestic fare sale ends April 25.</p>
<p>The international fares are discounted up to 39 percent and that sale ends April 28, TWA said.</p>
<p>All tickets must be purchased within three days of reservation and require a Saturday night stay.</p>
<p>Travel must be completed June 30 for John F. Kennedy airport nonstop flights and by August 30 for other flights, the airline said.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
